{{!-- Community sidebar: top topics, latest topics or latest posts from the Discourse
    forum. The "Community sidebar" theme setting turns it off or picks the
    list a first visit opens on; the heading lets visitors switch. The list is filled
    by assets/js/community-sidebar.js from the forum's public JSON, which needs
    CORS on the Discourse side (DISCOURSE_ENABLE_CORS plus this site in the
    "cors origins" setting). It shows from the first paint as rows of
    placeholders (aria-busy, community.css), so the posts never move when the
    forum answers; if it never does, the script hides it. Without scripting
    it never shows (html.js, set in <head> by theme.js).

    From 768px: a sticky column on the right. Phones: after the posts.

    category= (tag.hbs): only the topics of the forum category with that
    slug, without the picker; a tag with no category gets the whole forum's
    list, as /blog does. --}}
{{#if @custom.discourse_url}}{{#match @custom.community_sidebar "!=" "Off"}}
<aside class="gh-community" aria-labelledby="gh-community-title" aria-busy="true"
    data-category="{{category}}"
    data-mode="{{#match @custom.community_sidebar "Latest posts"}}posts{{else}}{{#match @custom.community_sidebar "Latest topics"}}topics{{else}}top{{/match}}{{/match}}"
    data-label-reply="{{t "reply"}}"
    data-label-replies="{{t "replies"}}"
    data-label-in="{{t "in"}}"
    data-label-back="{{t "← back"}}">
    {{!-- anonist, the forum's mascot, sitting on the box's top border on
        desktop (the "Community mascot" setting), or only his mask floating
        there (its "Mask" option); assets/js/mascot.js moves him and
        shows the phrase of the day on click. With a "Chat channel" set, his
        mask pops up from the chat tab instead (partials/chat.hbs). The sprite is
        generated by docs/frames.py in somos-criptonautas/discourse-nautas-mascot. --}}
    {{#match @custom.community_mascot "!=" "Off"}}{{#unless @custom.chat_channel}}
    <div class="gh-mascot{{#match @custom.community_mascot "Mask"}} is-mask{{/match}}" hidden>
        <p class="gh-mascot-bubble" role="status"></p>
        <button class="gh-mascot-button" type="button" aria-label="{{t "Phrase of the day"}}">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" shape-rendering="crispEdges" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="{{asset "images/anonist-sprite.svg"}}#anonist-48-{{#match @custom.community_mascot "Mask"}}mask-idle{{else}}sit{{/match}}"/></svg>
        </button>
    </div>
    {{/unless}}{{/match}}
    {{!-- "Comunidad" as the heading, with the list picker beside it:
        visitors switch between top topics, latest topics and replies, and the choice is
        remembered in their browser. The theme setting only picks which one a
        first visit opens on. --}}
    <div class="gh-community-head">
        <h2 class="gh-community-title" id="gh-community-title">
            {{t "Community"}}
        </h2>
        <span class="gh-community-picker">
            <select class="gh-community-select" aria-label="{{t "Community list"}}">
                <option value="top">{{t "Top stories"}}</option>
                <option value="topics">{{t "Topics"}}</option>
                <option value="posts">{{t "Replies"}}</option>
            </select>
            {{> "icons/phosphor/caret-down"}}
        </span>
    </div>
    <ol class="gh-community-list"></ol>
    <p class="gh-community-message" role="status" hidden>{{t "The community could not be loaded."}}</p>
    <a class="gh-community-more" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{t "Go to the community"}} {{> "icons/phosphor/arrow-square-out"}}</a>
</aside>
{{/match}}{{/if}}
